+/**
+ * @brief Precise vertices for the next polygon written to GP0
+ *
+ * Once called, every polygon command (GP0 20h-3Fh) written after it takes one
+ * entry, in order: call it once before each polygon. xyw holds x, y and w per
+ * vertex (n vertices, 3 or 4, as the command has); NULL (or n 0) leaves that
+ * polygon as its integer words give it. x and y replace the vertex's position
+ * (the same space: before the drawing offset), with subpixel precision; w > 0
+ * is its depth, for perspective-correct textures and colors (w 1: affine, as
+ * the PS1). Does nothing with a renderer without it.
+ */
+void Psyz_GpuPushPrecise(const float* xyw, int n);
